From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Map VC4 memory normal non-cacheable

The VC4 Gallium driver uses firmware allocations as identity-mapped CPU
pointers while V3D accesses the same physical storage. A write-through CPU
mapping does not make GPU writes coherent with cache lines already held by the
CPU. Use the existing Normal Non-Cacheable MAIR entry for the single canonical
mapping, matching the current AROS aarch64 V3D arena policy and the driver's
existing no-cache-maintenance contract.
---
 src/aarch64/start.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/aarch64/start.c b/src/aarch64/start.c
--- a/src/aarch64/start.c
+++ b/src/aarch64/start.c
@@ -1381,7 +1381,13 @@ void init_platform(void)
             };
             dt_add_property(dt_find_node("/emu68"), "vc4-mem", reg, 8);
 
-            mmu_map(vid_base, vid_base, vid_memory * 1024*1024, MMU_ACCESS | MMU_ISHARE | MMU_ALLOW_EL0 | MMU_ATTR_WRITETHROUGH, 0);
+            /*
+             * VC4 and the CPU share this identity-mapped firmware pool.
+             * Keep one canonical Normal Non-Cacheable view: write-through
+             * alone cannot make GPU writes visible over stale CPU lines.
+             */
+            mmu_map(vid_base, vid_base, vid_memory * 1024*1024,
+                    MMU_ACCESS | MMU_ISHARE | MMU_ALLOW_EL0 | MMU_ATTR_UNCACHED, 0);
         }
 
         if (unicam_base) {
